     "A clinical inbox triage case should be readable in one pass: the request, the evidence, the decision, and the next action belong in the same trail. Clinical Care Coordinator keeps clinical inbox triage bounded by an explicit close condition, so a finished item cannot hide an unresolved question behind a status label. If the team cannot tell whether clinical inbox triage is complete, the form is asking for description instead of evidence and should be revised before adding another review.",
     "The control earns trust when a new reviewer can repeat the same check and reach the same conclusion from the stored evidence. A weak clinical inbox triage process rewards speed without proof; a sound one records the source first and lets the clock measure the remaining work. The working rule for clinical inbox triage is simple: no source, no approval; no approval, no downstream change."
