     "Clinical Care Coordinator keeps clinical inbox triage evidence next to the decision so a later reviewer does not have to reconstruct the case from memory. When two clinical inbox triage records disagree, the record should show which source was preferred and who accepted that choice. The clinical inbox triage audit trail is not a transcript; it is a compact set of facts that proves the work was checked and the outcome was authorised.",
     "If the destination system cannot show the approved change, the clinical inbox triage case remains open even when the conversation feels finished. A useful clinical inbox triage note records the exception reason in plain language, because a generic code hides the pattern the team needs to fix. The clinical inbox triage entry should be short enough to complete at the point of work and specific enough to survive a later review."
